  • Stage 2: establish contract, translator identity, and independent differential tests
  • Stage 3: rebuild semantics/proof from clean source and run every positive claim
  • Stage 4: audit claim adequacy, real-program pinning, and concrete witnesses
  • Stage 5: inventory and review every syntax/function/rule/declaration
  • Stage 6: build and run a fresh meaningful false mutation
  • Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed facts and write final REVIEW.md
